      'NVDA spot 196.51, ATR 8.03, nearest zone a prior swing low at +0.18 ATR (band 193.95–201.99) — price is sitting essentially ON a level where it previously turned, less than a fifth of a typical day away. ⚠ Whether price reacts at these levels more often than chance is UNTESTED. Reference points for attention, not predictions.'),
  };


  // ── P-A: relative performance vs the market (twin of semiconductor.html) ────────────────────
  // Construction settled by measurement after the two reviewers disagreed: the RATIO (compounded
  // relative return), displayed as "% ahead/behind" so the reference sits at 0 rather than an
  // unexplained 100. On live data the difference-of-cumulatives diverges up to 4.70pp mid-window
  // on storage, so the difference form is not acceptable for a chart people will read off.
  // 2026-07-29: compute_sector_rs.py now emits the SAME ratio construction, so the chart and the
  // table agree exactly — the old "~1 point" reconciliation note has been removed from both
  // surfaces. Do NOT reintroduce a difference form on either side.
  // Palette: the dataviz-validated 4-hue dark set, NOT OC_CHART.COLORS — the terminal's own
